        "draftsman": "comfy-draftsman"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Models & LoRAs\n\nSwap models here to change the whole look.\n\nThree parts plus a second VAE. UNETLoader for the\ndiffusion model, CLIPLoader with type=minimax for the\nQwen3-VL 32B encoder, VAELoader for the VIDEO vae, and\na SECOND VAELoader for the AUDIO vae. H3 emits a joint\nvideo+audio latent: decode it twice (VAEDecode with\nthe video vae, VAEDecodeAudio with the audio vae) and\nre-mux with CreateVideo at 24 fps.\n\n| knob | now | range / choices | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| strength_model | 1 | -100.0-100.0 | How strongly the LoRA affects the diffusion model - higher is a stronger stylistic pull, can overpower the base model. |"
      ],
      "title": "Models & LoRAs",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 203,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1665.0,
        -365.0
      ],
      "size": [
        380.0,
        325.0
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "draftsman": "comfy-draftsman"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Sampling\n\nReference template uses res_multistep / simple, 20\nsteps, denoise 1.0, via BasicGuider +\nSamplerCustomAdvanced. MiniMaxH3SigmaShift\n(shift_video 12.0, shift_audio 3.0) exists but the\nreference template does NOT use it - leave it bypassed\nunless motion flow is visibly wrong.\n\nFamily reference: steps 12-50.\n\n| knob | now | range / choices | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| scheduler (BasicScheduler #120) | simple |  | Changes how noise is removed across steps - pairs with sampler_name; some samplers expect a specific scheduler. |\n| steps (BasicScheduler #120) | *(wired)* | | |\n| denoise (BasicScheduler #120) | 1 | 0.0-1.0 | Higher denoise changes the image more (closer to a fresh generation); lower preserves more of the input. |\n| noise_seed (RandomNoise #125) | 1 |  | Same seed + same settings = same result. Change it for a new variation; keep it fixed to iterate on one image. |\n| sampler_name (KSamplerSelect #127) | res_multistep |  | Changes the sampling algorithm - affects speed and sharpness, and how much a given step count buys you. |"
      ],
      "title": "Sampling",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
